h is 74 times 100. Either way, the answer is 7400. \n\nI can't see any mistakes in this reasoning. All the different methods confirm that the product is 7400. So, I'm confident that's the correct answer.\n\n<|end_of_thought|>\n\n<|begin_of_solution|>\n\nThe product of \\(74\\) and \\(100\\) is calculated by recognizing that multiplying by \\(100\\) adds two zeros to the end of the number. Thus, \\(74 \\times 100 = 7400\\). \n\n\\(\\boxed{7400}\\)\n\n<|end_of_solution|>",
