product of 32 and 46 is calculated as follows:\n\n1. **Break down the multiplication**:\n   - \\(30 \\times 46 = 1380\\) (since \\(30 \\times 40 = 1200\\) and \\(30 \\times 6 = 180\\), summing to 1380)\n   - \\(2 \\times 46 = 92\\) (since \\(40 \\times 2 = 80\\) and \\(6 \\times 2 = 12\\), summing to 92)\n\n2. **Add the results**:\n   - \\(1380 + 92 = 1472\\)\n\n**Verification**:\n- Using the distributive property: \\(32 \\times 46 = 30 \\times 46 + 2 \\times 46 = 1380 + 92 = 1472\\)\n- Direct multiplication: \\(32 \\times 46 = 1472\\)\n\nThe final answer is \\(\\boxed{1472}\\).\n\n<|end_of_solution|>",
