uct of two numbers where one is a multiple of 10. Let me recall. If one number is 10 times another, then the product is 10 times the product of the other number and 10. So, if one number is 24, which is 10 times 2.4, then the product is 10 \u00d7 (2.4 \u00d7 42). Then, 2.4 \u00d7 42 is 1008, so 10 \u00d7 1008 = 10080. But 24 \u00d7 42 is 1008, which is 10080 divided by 10. So, 10080 / 10 = 1008. So, that's another way to get the same answer. So, that's a quicker method.\n\nAlternatively, maybe using the formula for the product of two numbers where one is a multiple of 10. Let me think. If one number is 10 times another, then the product is 10 times the product of the other number and 10. So, if one number is 24, which is 10 times 2.4, then the product is 10 \u00d7 (2.4 \u00d7 42). Then, 2.4 \u00d7 42 is 1008, so 10 \u00d7 1008 = 10080. But 24 \u00d7 42 is 1008, which is 10080 divided by 10. So, 10080 / 10 = 1008. So, that's another way to get the same answer. So, that's a quicker method.\n\nAlternatively, maybe using the formula for the product of two numbers where one is a multiple of 10. Let me recall. If one number is 10 times another, then the product is 10 times the product of the other number and 10. So, if one number is 24, which is 10 times 2.4, then the product is 10 \u00d7 (2.4 \u00d7 42). Then, 2.4 \u00d7 42 is 1008, so 10 \u00d7 1008 = 10080. But 24 \u00d7 42 is 1008, which is 10080 divided by 10. So, 10080 / 10 = 1008. So, that's another way to get the same answer. So, that's a quicker method.\n\nAlternatively, maybe using the formula for the product of two numbers where one is a multiple of 10. Let me think. If one number is 10 times another, then the product is 10 times the product of the other number and 10. So, if one number is 24, which is 10 times 2.4, then the product is 10 \u00d7 (2.4 \u00d7 42). Then, 2.4 \u00d7 42 is 1008, so 10 \u00d7 1008 = 10080. But 24 \u00d7 42 is 1008, which is 10080 divided by 10. So, 10080 / 10 = 1008. So, that's anoth