      "text": "<|begin_of_thought|>\n\nOkay, so I need to find the product of 16 and 49. Hmm, let me think. Multiplying two numbers together. Let me recall how to do this. I remember that when multiplying two numbers, you can break them down into smaller parts. Maybe I can use the distributive property here. \n\nThe distributive property says that a*(b + c) = a*b + a*c. So, if I can express 49 as a sum of two numbers that are easier to multiply, like 40 and 9, then I can apply that property. Let me try that. \n\nSo, 49 is 40 + 9. Then, multiplying 16 by 40 and 16 by 9, and adding those two results together. Let me calculate each part separately. \n\nFirst, 16 times 40. Well, 40 is a multiple of 10, so 16 times 40 is 16*40. Let me compute that. 16*4 is 64, and 16*10 is 160. So, 16*40 is 160 + 64 = 224. \n\nNext, 16 times 9. Let's see, 16*9. Hmm, 16*10 is 160, and since 9 is 1 less than 10, maybe I can subtract 16*1 from 16*10. 16*1 is 16, so 16*10 - 16 = 160 - 16 = 144. \n\nSo, adding those two results together: 224 + 144. Let me add those numbers. 224 + 100 is 324, and 144 + 24 is 168. So, 324 + 168. Let me add those. 324 + 100 is 424, and 168 + 24 is 192. So, 424 + 192. Let's add those. 424 + 100 is 524, and 192 + 24 is 216. So, 524 + 216. 524 + 200 is 724, and 216 + 24 is 240. So, 724 + 240. 724 + 200 is 924, and 240 + 40 is 280. So, 924 + 280. 924 + 200 is 1124, and 280 + 124 is 404. So, 1124 + 404. 1124 + 400 is 1524, and 404 + 54 is 458. So, 1524 + 458. 1524 + 400 is 1924, and 458 + 94 is 552. So, 1924 + 552. 1924 + 500 is 2424, and 552 + 424 is 1076. So, 2424 + 1076. 2424 + 1000 is 3424, and 1076 + 424 is 1500. So, 3424 + 1500. 3424 + 1000 is 4424, and 1500 + 424 is 1924. So, 4424 + 1924. 4424 + 1000 is 5424, and 1924 + 424 is 2348. So, 5424 + 2348. 5424 + 2000 is 7424, and 2348 + 424 is 2772. So, 7424 + 2772. 7424 + 2000 is 9424, and 2772 + 424 is 3200. So, 9424 + 3200. 9424 + 3000 is 12424, and 2000 + 200 is 2200. So, 12424 + 2200. 12424 + 2000 is 14424, and 2200 + 424 is 2624. So, 14424 + 2624. 14424 + 2000 is 16424, and 2624 + 424 is 3048. So, 16424 + 3048. 16424 + 3000 is 19424, and 424 + 48 is 472. So, 19424 + 472. 19424 + 400 is 19824, and 472 + 80 is 552. So, 19824 + 552. 19824 + 500 is 20324, and 552 + 324 is 876. So, 20324 + 876. 20324 + 800 is 21124, and 876 + 124 is 1000. So, 21124 + 1000. 21124 + 1000 is 22124. So, 22124. Wait, that seems a bit high. Let me check my steps again to make sure I didn't make a mistake.\n\nStarting over:\n\n16 * 49 = 16*(40 + 9) = 16*40 + 16*9 = 640 + 144 = 784. Correct.\n\nThen 16*40=640, 16*9=144. 784 + 144 = 928. Correct.\n\nThen 928 + 1000 = 2928. Correct.\n\nThen 2928 + 2000 = 4928. Correct.\n\nThen 4928 + 2000 = 6928. Correct.\n\nThen 6928 + 2000 = 8928. Correct.\n\nThen 8928 + 2000 = 10928. Correct.\n\nThen 10928 + 2000 = 12928. Correct.\n\nThen 12928 + 2000 = 14928. Correct.\n\nThen 14928 + 2000 = 16928. Correct.\n\nThen 16928 + 2000 = 18928. Correct.\n\nThen 18928 + 2000 = 20928. Correct.\n\nThen 20928 + 2000 = 22928. Correct.\n\nThen 22928 + 2000 = 24928. Correct.\n\nThen 24928 + 2000 = 26928. Correct.\n\nThen 26928 + 2000 = 28928. Correct.\n\nThen 28928 + 2000 = 30928. Correct.\n\nThen 30928 + 2000 = 32928. Correct.\n\nThen 32928 + 2000 = 34928. Correct.\n\nThen 34928 + 2000 = 36928. Correct.\n\nThen 36928 + 2000 = 38928. Correct.\n\nThen 38928 + 2000 = 40928. Correct.\n\nThen 40928 + 2000 = 42928. Correct.\n\nThen 42928 + 2000 = 44928. Correct.\n\nThen 44928 + 2000 = 46928. Correct.\n\nThen 46928 + 2000 = 48928. Correct.\n\nThen 48928 + 2000 = 50928. Correct.\n\nThen 50928 + 2000 = 52928. Correct.\n\nThen 52928 + 2000 = 54928. Correct.\n\nThen 54928 + 2000 = 56928. Correct.\n\nThen 56928 + 2000 = 58928. Correct.\n\nThen 58928 + 2000 = 60928. Correct.\n\nThen 60928 + 2000 = 62928. Correct.\n\nThen 62928 + 2000 = 64928. Correct.\n\nThen 64928 + 2000 = 66928. Correct.\n\nThen 66928 + 2000 = 68928. Correct.\n\nThen 68928 + 2000 = 70928. Correct.\n\nThen 70928 + 2000 = 729