re. So both methods give 3986. That seems consistent. \n\nAlternatively, maybe I can use the formula for the product of two numbers. For two numbers a and b, the product is a*b = (a + b)(a - b) + 4ab. Wait, maybe that's a different approach. Let me check. \n\nWait, the formula is (a + b)(a - b) + 4ab. Let me verify that. \n\nIf a = 67 and b = 58, then (67 + 58)(67 - 58) + 4*67*58. \n\nCalculating (67 + 58) is 125, and (67 - 58) is 9. So 125*9 is 1125. Then, 4*67*58. Let's compute that. \n\nFirst, 67*58. Let's do 60*58 = 3480, and 7*58 = 406. So 3480 + 406 = 3886. Then, 4*3886 = 15544. \n\nSo adding 1125 and 15544. Let's compute that. 1125 + 15544. 15544 + 10000 is 25544, then +125 is 25669. \n\nWait, that's different from the previous result. So that formula gives 25669, which is different from 3986. So that's a problem. \n\nWait, maybe I made a mistake in the formula. Let me check again. \n\nThe formula is (a + b)(a - b) + 4ab. Let's verify with a = 67, b = 58. \n\n(a + b)(a - b) = 125, and 4ab = 4*67*58. Let's compute 67*58 first. \n\n67*50 = 3350, 67*8 = 536. So 3350 + 536 = 3886. Then, 4*3886 = 15544. \n\nSo (125 + 3886) + 15544. 125 + 3886 is 4011, and 4011 + 15544 = 19555. \n\nBut according to the formula, it's supposed to be 3986. So that's a contradiction. \n\nWait, that can't be right. So where did I go wrong? \n\nWait, maybe the formula is different. Let me check the formula again. \n\nThe formula is (a + b)(a - b) + 4ab. Let's compute (a + b)(a - b) first. \n\n(a + b)(a - b) = a\u00b2 - b\u00b2. \n\nThen, 4ab. So total product is a\u00b2 - b\u00b2 + 4ab. \n\nSo for a = 67, b = 58, then a\u00b2 - b\u00b2 + 4ab = 67\u00b2 - 58\u00b2 + 4*67*58. \n\nCalculating 67\u00b2: 67*67. Let's compute 60\u00b2 = 3600, 7\u00b2 = 49, so 3600 + 49 = 3649. \n\n58\u00b2: 50\u00b2 = 2500, 8\u00b2 = 64, so 2500 + 64 = 2564. \n\nThen, 4*67*58. Let's compute 67*58 first. 60*58 = 3480, 7*58 = 406, so 3480 + 406 = 3886. \n\nSo total is 3649 - 2564 + 3886. \n\n3649 - 2564 = 1085. 